  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed building, by virtue of its height, detailed design, form, siting, bulk, pattern of fenestration, would appear visually intrusive, incongruous, overly dominant and out of keeping with the character and appearance of the streetscene and the surrounding area of which it forms part, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3, D4, D5, D8 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD8, DMD12 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its height, orientation, form, siting, bulk, pattern of fenestration, alignment, width, proximity to the site boundary would give rise to an unneighbourly loss of privacy, sunlight and daylight, outlook, as perceived from neighbouring properties, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D3, D4, D5, D6, D8 of the London Plan (2021), CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD8, DMD10 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of an adequate flood risk assessment and sustainable drainage strategy, fails to demonstrate how proposed measures manage the risk of flooding and utilise Sustainable Urban Drainage Systems (SuDS) following the drainage hierarchy in the London Plan, contrary to Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), CP21 and CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD59, DMD60, DMD61, DMD62 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the Enfield Strategic Flood Risk Assessment (2021)."
  ],
